Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  19 AUG 98 at 14 46 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2 TO FOCALLY 3  SINGLE FOCUS SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  AND PRESENT AT OR WITHIN LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS AND PRESENT AT OR WITHIN LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM  FROM THE RESECTION MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of lymphatic vessels and blood vessels is not seen  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  21 AUG 98 at 17 24                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 AUG 98 at 09 20     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast  is a breast biopsy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm with a needle localization wire in place  A firm 2 1cm mass is filled within the specimen  The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal a white infiltrative mass within  1 0mm from inked margin  Representative sections are in A C  Resident  ADRIANO PIRIS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , No.
