Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 56 CLINICAL DATA  Non palpable right breast cancer on sterotactic core from outside hospital                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  BREAST  RIGHT    ADDITIONAL MARGIN   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 17 OF 17 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 19                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  number only is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of breast with a localizing needle and accompanying specimen X ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal a firm white stellate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm lesion extending to within 0 5cm of the closest inked margin  A representative section is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Sections of mass are submitted in cassettes A B  Representative sections of breast  submitted in cassettes C E  A portion of the lesion is taken by Dr  Deutch  Received in two container  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm aggregate mass of adipose tissue and lymph nodes  Lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes F through Q  Labeled  additional margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE unoriented piece of breast tissue  Sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes R through T  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING MAMMARY CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PARTIAL MASTECTOMY PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES PART C  ROGHT BREAST  ADDITIONAL MARGIN   report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 AUG 95 ACCESSIONED ON  01 AUG 95 at 12 07 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  SOLID PAPILLARY CARCINOMA  IN SITU AND INVASIVE  GRADE II III  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE   2  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  Lymphatic and blood vascular invasion is not seen  The tumor displays features of endocrine differentiation  Due to the lobulated architecture of the tumor  the distinction between in situ and infiltrating carcinoma is difficult and percentages of each cannot be easily assessed  Substantial amounts of both components are present  Immunoperoxidase stains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be performed and the results reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  04 AUG 95 at 16 26 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 95 at 15 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fragment of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm firm mass  within 0 4cm of the closest resection margin  The remaining tissue is unremarkable  Three sections from the nodule including surrounding margin are submitted in cassettes A through C  a section 2 0cm away from the nodule is submitted in cassette D  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION  REMOVED_DATE CM NODULE THAT IS SUGGESTIVE OF INVASIVE TUMOR  WITH SUSPICIOUS CELLS ON TOUCH PREPORATION  DIAGNOSIS DEFERRED TO FINAL HISTOLOGICAL SECTIONS  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Andrew Louis Warshaw  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , No.
