Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 02 CLINICAL DATA  The patient presents with a new left breast mass with positive cytology on fine needle aspiration at the MGH                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  PARTIAL MASTECTOMY   1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  1 8 CM   POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE III III   FOCALLY EXTENDING TO LESS THAN ONE HIGH POWER FIELD OF THE SUPERIOR INKED MARGIN AND LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE DEEP INKED MARGIN  WITH SEVERAL FOCI HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE   2  TUBULAR CARCINOMA  1 1 CM   INVASIVE  LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED ANTEROMEDIAL SURFACE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The specimen contains two separate primary infiltrating ductal carcinomas  These two carcinomas have distinct cytoarchitectural features  Blood vascular invasion is not seen  3  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  CRIBRIFORM AND COMEDO TYPE  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  4  FIBROADENOMA  5  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  AXILLARY CONTENTS   LEFT AXILLARY TISSUE  A  AND  C     METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The metastases consist of several   10  small aggregates of malignant cells confined to the subcapsular sinus in a small region of the lymph node  The metastasis is less than 0 1cm in size  BREAST   ADDITIONAL BREAST MARGINS   ANTEROMEDIAL   ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  MULTIFOCAL  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM SEVERAL INKED SURFACES INCLUDING THE MEDIAL AND SUPERIOR INKED SURFACES  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 19 38                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  both nodules   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received in four separately labeled parts  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm left partial mastectomy specimen  with sutures marking the lateral and superior aspects of the specimen  There is no skin ellipse  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  ellipsoid  well demarcated  firm  white nodule  The nodule is located 0 4cm from the superior margin  slide A   0 4cm from the deep margin  slide B   0 7cm from the anterior margin  slide C   1 1cm from the inferior margin  slide D   2 0cm from the lateral margin  slide E  en face   and 2 5cm from the medial margin  A second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  firm  gritty  white nodule is located 0 1cm from the anterior margin  frozen  section is taken from this nodule and saved for hormone receptor studies   0 7cm from the medial margin  slide G  en face   1 0cm from the deep margin  slide F  with yellow ink   1 5cm from the inferior margin  slide F  with blue ink   2 5cm from the superior margin  and 5 0cm from the lateral margin  Both nodules are surrounded by freely mobile unremarkable breast parenchyma  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Additional breast margins   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with sutures marking the superior and medial aspects of the specimen  The medial aspect is inked in black  the superior aspect is inked in blue  and the remainder is inked in yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned inferior to superior and submitted entirely in cassettes H through O  respectively  Received in formalin  labeled  Left axillary tissue  A    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of three portions of fibroadipose tissue containing lymph nodes  The specimen is submitted entirely as P  Received in formalin  labeled  Left axillary contents  C    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm portion of adipose tissue containing ten lymph nodes  ranging in diameter from REMOVED_DATE to 1 3cm  The lymph nodes are submitted in Q S  SECTION CODE  A  larger nodule with superior margin  B  larger nodule with deep margin  C  larger nodule with anterior margin  D  larger nodule with inferior margin  E  lateral margin  F  smaller nodule  corresponding to nodule from which frozen section was taken  with anterior  inferior  and deep margins  G  medial margin  H O  additional breast margins   anteromedial  P S  lymph nodes  Resident