s not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 07 46 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a mastectomy specimen weighing 560 grams and measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm  There is a stitch denoting the 12 o clock position of the specimen  The anterior skin surface measures REMOVED_DATE x 4 2cm with a nipple areola complex measuring 2 5cm in diameter  The nipple appears diffusely ulcerated and erythematous  However  there is no mass grossly identified underneath the nipple  The nipple is cross sectioned to reveal scattered underlying hemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue  Representative sections of the ulcerated nipple are submitted in cassettes A B  The entire resected surface is black inked and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm mass at 12 o clock adjacent to  but not involving intact breast prosthesis  The breast mass is irregularly circumscribed  gritty  tan  and firm and is approximately 0 9cm from the closest anterior margin  The mass is approximately 2 2cm from the closest posterior margin  Representative sections of the mass and the anterior margin are submitted into cassettes C F  A representative section of the closest posterior margin to this mass is submitted into cassette G  Further sectioning reveals a separate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm irregularly circumscribed breast mass present at the 11 o clock posterior portion of the specimen  This mass appears to approach the posterior margin to within 0 2cm  Representative sections of this mass with the closest posterior margin are submitted into cassettes H I and representative sections of this mass with the closest anterior margin are submitted into cassettes J K  There is also an irregular thickening of the breast at the 1 o clock pos