Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 18 CLINICAL DATA  Abnormal mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  75    REMOVED_DATE IN DIAMETER IN HISTOLOGIC SECTION  EXTENDING TO INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  25    WIDESPREAD  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA   NOTE  No definite lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  Immunohistochemical stains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be reported in an addendum  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  B  BREAST  LEFT DEEP MARGIN  BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  PRESENT AT INKED AND CAUTERIZED MARGIN  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  Diagnosis by  Anthony Mattia  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 33                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Deep margin  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of white to tan fibroadipose tissue  submitted entirely in A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire in place  A roentgenogram accompanies this specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm  irregular lesion  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm in greatest dimension  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the tissue is submitted entirely in B through L  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST LESION   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Kathleen O Neil Smith  BUMS O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY PART B  DEEP MARGIN  LEFT BREAST    report_end  , No.
