Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 47 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  PREDOMINANTLY TUBULAR TYPE   80    EXTENDING TO AN INKED MARGIN OF EXCISION  SEE NOTE  2  EXTENSIVE FAT NECROSIS  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Greater than 95  of the tumor is infiltrating  No vascular of lymphatic invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 39                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT  LUMPECTOMY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   3   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  16 AUG 93 at 09 13     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 AUG 93 at 09 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is one piece of unoriented fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal fibrofatty tissue consistent with breast parenchyma  and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan nodule with an ill defined border within 4mm of the inked resection margin  Representative section as frozen section  1  Remaining lesional tissue in A  Remaining breast as B through N  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  James Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Kane  MD PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , No.
