Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 01 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  SCANT  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 21 59                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of breast with an incision into the specimen  The specimen is inked such that only the true margins bear ink  Inspection reveals an approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm tan  firm  lobulated  well circumscribed mass with central and eccentric white stellate lesion which grossly approaches several margins  The tissue surrounding the mass is white and irregularly dense  Entire mass and representative surrounding tissue are submitted in cassettes A J  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST MASS  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 33 CLINICAL DATA  29 year old female with right breast carcinoma  grade III  and left breast ductal carcinoma in situ  Status post left lumpectomy with positive margins                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  COMEDO TYPE  EXTENSIVELY PRESENT ON 7 OF 8 SECTIONS  WITH A MAXIMUM MEASURED SPAN OF REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE TO MULTIPLE MARGINS  Note  No stromal  lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL LATERAL    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  EXTENSIVELY PRESENT ON 4 OF 5 SECTIONS  WITH A MAXIMUM MEASURED SPAN OF REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE NEW  TRUE  MARGINS  Note  No stromal  lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 25                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Two specimens are received fresh  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Designated  left breast tumor  long stitch lateral  is an oriented 6 x 4 x 2 5cm breast tissue with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm skin ellipse  with a short and long stitch  There is a 1 6cm well healed scar in the skin ellipse  The entire excised surface is inked black  and over inked according to the following  superior  blue  lateral  red  medial  yellow  and inferior  green  Cross sectioning reveals a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm biopsy cavity filled with red brown  gelatinous material  The tissue on one side of the biopsy cavity is firm and fibrous  diffusely extending into the surrounding breast parenchyma  The other side has yellow white  opaque discoloration  forming a 1cm rim along the biopsy cavity  The biopsy appears to extend to the inferior excised margin  This margin is in A  Sections from the biopsy cavity are in B through G  Parenchyma away from biopsy cavity is in H  Designated  additional lateral tissue  long equals new lateral margin  short equals superior  is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm fragment of breast tissue with a long and short stitch  The new lateral excised surface is inked black  and the medial inked red  Cross sectioning reveals firm  white tissue with cystic changes admixed with adipose tissue  Fully submitted in I through M  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael V Seiden  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL LATERAL    EXCISIONAL BIO PART B  BREAST  LEFT TUMOR   EXCISION   report_end  , No.
