Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 22 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  65   WELL TO MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  35   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The infiltrating tumor component extends to within 0 1cm to the inked margin  and the intraductal component is focally less than 0 1cm from the inked margin  The tumor measures 1 2cm in greatest dimension on paraffin embedded tissue  There is no unequivocal evidence of lymphatic or vascular invasion  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE  FLORID  3  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 18 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinel