X  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  NOTE  No definitive lymphovascular invasion is seen  The cervix and serosa are not involved by tumor  The examined resection margins are negative  OVARY AND FALLOPIAN TUBE  RIGHT   SALPINGO OOPHORECTOMY  1  OVARY  EPITHELIAL INCLUSION GLANDS  2  FALLOPIAN TUBE  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  OVARY AND FALLOPIAN TUBE  LEFT   SALPINGO OOPHORECTOMY  1  OVARY  EPITHELIAL INCLUSION GLANDS  2  FALLOPIAN TUBE  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT OBTURATOR   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 7 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT EXTERNAL PELVIC   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 7 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODE  LEFT OBTURATOR   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODES  LEFT EXTERNAL ILIAC   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 10 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Dr  Melinda Lerwill reviewed the breast specimens  and Dr  Esther Oliva reviewed the gynecologic specimens  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Woods  REMOVE_MRN and  right sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of yellow lobulated adipose tissue  in which a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm pink rubbery lymph node is identified  The lymph node is bisected and submitted in its entirety as frozen section as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled Woods  Joan  REMOVE_MRN  and  right lumpectomy   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm oriented portion of tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a short stitch designating superior  a long stitch designating lateral margin  and two needle localization wire in place  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse which contains REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm nipple  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial to lateral axis to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan pink to tan white  firm  ill defined and focally cystic mass which lies 0 2cm from the posterior  1 5cm from the inferior  5 0cm from the anterior  3 0cm from the superior  2 0cm from the lateral  and 5 0cm from the medial margins  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan white  ill defined firm area which lies 0 6cm medial and anterior to the first fairly well defined mass and lies 2 0cm from the posterior  2 5cm from the inferior  4 0cm from the superior  4 5cm from the anterior  3 0cm from the lateral  and 4 0cm from the medial margins  The rest of the breast parenchyma displays a tan yellow lobulated cut surface and contains a focal cluster of cystic spaces which extrude the tan brown pasty material on pressure  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire first tan pink irregular mass to include closest inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire thickened tan pink irregular mass to include closest inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Intervening nodular breast parenchyma between the first and second mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  focally cystic breast parenchyma away from mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   En face section  medial margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   En face section  lateral margin  Received are seven containers which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  uterus  cervix   is a 211 gram hysterectomy specimen which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm  The posterior cervical margin is inked black  and the anterior cervical margin is inked blue  Opening the specimen reveals a large REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 7cm solid tan white mass with an epicenter in the upper portion of the myometrium to involve both the anterior and posterior aspects of the myometrium  This mass causes a 5 7cm exophytic protrusion into the anterior and posterior endomyometrium  The mass is very homogeneous with an only 1 0cm greatest dimension area of hemorrhage and very rare areas which are darker yellow  0 1cm in greatest dimension   Overall the mass does not display areas of softening or necrosis  There is a distinct border between the mass and the normal appearing myometrium  The mass involves almost the entire width of the myometrium and depth wise comes to within 0 4cm of the serosa in places  The boundary of the mass with the overlying endometrium is blurred with a suggestion of a 0 1cm thick endometrium overlying the mass  The exophytic portion of this mass which protrudes the endometrial cavity is  3 0cm from both the anterior and posterior lower uterine segment  The endometrium distal to the mass shows focal roughening and appears to be  0 1cm in thickness  The myometrium in the uninvolved portion of the specimen is up to 1 1cm in thickness  The mucosa of the cervix displays a tan pink herringbone like appearance and is unremarkable  The serosa of the specimen is smooth  The following sections are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative full cross section of the mass with its relation to the endometrium  myometrium and serosa as diagrammed   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections displaying the relationship of the mass to the overlying endometrium   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of the mass including the area of hemorrhage and the darker speckled yellow areas   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Full thickness representative section of the posterior cervix   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative full thickness section from the posterior LUS   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Full thickness representative section from the anterior cervix   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Full thickness